---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — eKosha"
  description="Learn how eKosha collects, uses and protects your personal information in accordance with the DPDP Act 2023."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-24">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-brand-muted mb-1 text-sm">Last updated: November 24, 2026</p>
    <p class="text-brand-muted mb-10 text-sm">Effective date: November 24, 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Policy version: 1.2</p>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-brand-navy mb-3">About eKosha</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed">
        eKosha ("we", "our", "us") is a family financial preparedness application that helps you organise important financial information and share it with the people you trust.
        We are committed to protecting your personal data in accordance with the
        <strong>Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (DPDP Act)</strong> and other applicable laws.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-brand-navy mb-3">1. Data We Collect</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm text-brand-text border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-brand-bg">
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-brand-navy border border-brand-navy/10">Category</th>
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-brand-navy border border-brand-navy/10">Examples</th>
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-brand-navy border border-brand-navy/10">Purpose</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Identity data</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Full name, date of birth, gender</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Create and maintain your profile</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-brand-bg/50">
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Contact data</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Email address, phone number</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Account authentication, notifications</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Asset data</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Financial account details, insurance policies, property records, nominee and co-owner details</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Core service — asset vault</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-brand-bg/50">
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Documents you attach</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Policy PDFs, deed photos, statements</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Kept with the asset they belong to; stored encrypted</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Documents you choose to import</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">A document or mutual fund / demat statement you pick for "Import from document"</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Read once to pre-fill an entry for you to review. Statement files and their passwords are not stored</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-brand-bg/50">
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Usage data</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Feature interactions, session timestamps</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Improve app performance</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Device data</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Device type, OS version</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Crash reporting, compatibility</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-brand-navy mb-3">2. How We Use Your Data</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed mb-3">We process your data solely for the purposes to which you have consented:</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 text-brand-text text-sm leading-relaxed">
        <li><strong>Profile &amp; Asset Data</strong> — to provide, operate, and maintain the eKosha service.</li>
        <li><strong>Cross-Border Transfer</strong> — your database and application servers are hosted in <strong>India (Mumbai)</strong> on Google Firebase. Some supporting services process limited data outside India: in the United States (Resend, RevenueCat, and Google's authentication, crash reporting and performance services), in the European Union — Frankfurt, Germany (PostHog), and, only when you choose AI document reading, by Google's Gemini service. See Sections 3 and 4.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics</strong> <em>(optional)</em> — to understand how users interact with the app and improve features.</li>
        <li><strong>Marketing Notifications</strong> <em>(optional)</em> — to inform you about new features, tips, and promotions.</li>
        <li><strong>AI document reading</strong> <em>(only when you use it)</em> — when you choose to import a photo or PDF (other than a mutual fund or demat statement), its content is sent once to Google's Gemini service under a no-training agreement, used to pre-fill the entry form, and not stored there. Nothing is saved until you review and confirm it. You are asked for your permission before first use and can turn it off in Settings.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-brand-navy mb-3">3. Data Sharing and Processors</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed mb-4">
        We share your data only with the following processors, and only as necessary. Each service does one job only. We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal data to any third party, and we do not show advertising.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm text-brand-text border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-brand-bg">
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-brand-navy border border-brand-navy/10">Processor</th>
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-brand-navy border border-brand-navy/10">Country</th>
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-brand-navy border border-brand-navy/10">Purpose</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Google Firebase (database, application servers)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">India (Mumbai)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Storing your account and asset data and running eKosha</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-brand-bg/50">
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Google Firebase (authentication, crash reporting, push messaging, performance &amp; diagnostics monitoring)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">United States</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Sign-in, stability, notifications; performance monitoring is optional and consent-based</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Google Gemini</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Outside India (determined by Google)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">AI document reading — only when you choose to use it</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-brand-bg/50">
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Resend</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">United States</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Transactional email delivery</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">RevenueCat</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">United States</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">In-app subscription management (Android)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-brand-bg/50">
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Razorpay</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">India</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Subscription payments on the web</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">PostHog</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">European Union (Frankfurt, Germany)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border border-brand-navy/10">Product analytics (optional, consent-based)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-brand-navy mb-3">4. Cross-Border Data Transfer</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed">
        Your account and asset data is stored on Google Firebase in <strong>India (Mumbai)</strong>. Limited data is processed outside India by the following services:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-brand-text mt-3 mb-3">
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-gold font-bold shrink-0">·</span><span>AES-256-GCM encryption of sensitive asset details, asset titles and attached documents before they are stored.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-gold font-bold shrink-0">·</span><span>Contact details such as names and email addresses are separately encrypted.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-gold font-bold shrink-0">·</span><span>Security rules that check who you are on every request, so records are opened only for you and the people you have shared them with.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-gold font-bold shrink-0">·</span><span>PIN / biometric lock on mobile devices.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-gold font-bold shrink-0">·</span><span>Audit logs of important actions and changes.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-brand-navy mb-3">8. Children's Data</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed">
        eKosha is intended for users <strong>18 years of age and older</strong>. We do not knowingly collect personal data from minors.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-brand-navy mb-3">9. Grievance Officer</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed">
        In accordance with Section 13 of the DPDP Act 2023, we have designated a Grievance Officer. You may contact them at:
      </p>
      <div class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-text space-y-1">
        <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:grievance@ekosha.co.in" class="text-brand-gold underline">grievance@ekosha.co.in</a></p>
        <p><strong>Designation:</strong> Privacy Team, eKosha</p>
        <p><strong>Response time:</strong> Within 30 days of receipt of your complaint.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-brand-navy mb-3">10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed">
        We will notify you of any material changes to this policy through the app. Continued use after notification constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
        Where required by law, we will seek fresh consent.
      </p>
      <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed mt-3">
        This version (<strong>1.2</strong>) states that your database and application servers are hosted in India (Mumbai), corrects the list of services that process limited data outside India, and adds Razorpay (web payments), Google Gemini (AI document reading, only when you choose it), and document attachments and statement import to this policy. Because the cross-border disclosure has changed, all users are asked to review and accept the updated consent in-app before continuing to use eKosha.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-brand-navy mb-3">11. Contact Us</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed">
        For privacy-related questions, email us at{' '}
        <a href="mailto:privacy@ekosha.co.in" class="text-brand-gold underline">privacy@ekosha.co.in</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
